From d37a68536d82b43b52bfa18a4117c36ae51d3104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vbardales <virginie.bardales@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:38:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(steps): say what a click met when the window it
 should open does not

`window {string} is open` failed with "open windows: ImmediateWindow,
ImmediateWindow", which identifies nothing. When the scenario has clicked,
the message now adds the tag clicked, the rect Pickle recorded for it, the
pointer before and after the click and now, every ButtonText drawn under the
pointer in draw order, and the window stack top first with each window's
type, assembly, layer, rect, absorbInputAroundWindow, GetsInput, whether it
holds the pointer and, for an ImmediateWindow, the method that draws it.

It is a diagnostic: it states what it saw and names no cause. The logic that
formats it sits in Pickle.Core and is unit tested; the game side only
gathers the inputs. PickleContext.DescribeLastClick() exposes it to other
steps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
