index 1df0902..8d042db 100644
--- a/Docs/steps.md
+++ b/Docs/steps.md
@@ -519,7 +519,7 @@ while a follow is active.
 | `I select {string}` | Selects a pawn or thing by name |
 | `I open the {string} tab` | Opens a main tab by def name or label |
 | `I close all dialogs` | Closes every open window |
-| `window {string} is open` | Checks a window type is open |
+| `window {string} is open` | Checks a window type is open. After a click, a failure also reports where the click went, see [a click that opened nothing](#a-click-that-opened-nothing) |
 | `window {string} is closed` | Checks a window type is closed |
 | `the inspect pane shows {string}` | Checks the selected thing's label |
 | `no errors were logged` | Fails if the game logged an error during the scenario |
@@ -569,3 +569,24 @@ PickleUI.Tag("my-button", buttonRect);
 
 Vanilla buttons need no tagging. Pickle records them by label, so
 `I click button "Research"` works out of the box.
+
+## A click that opened nothing
+
+A click can open nothing for reasons the step cannot see from the outside, and
+`window {string} is open` then fails with a list of type names. Several windows can share a type
+name, `ImmediateWindow` above all, so the list identifies nothing.
+
+When the scenario has clicked before the step fails, the message adds what that click met:
+
+- The tag clicked, the rect Pickle had recorded for it, and the pointer before the click, after it,
+  and now.
+- Every control drawn under the pointer in the last frame, in draw order.
+- The window stack, top first. Each window shows its type and assembly, its layer and rect,
+  `absorbInputAroundWindow`, `WindowStack.GetsInput`, whether its rect holds the pointer, and, for
+  an `ImmediateWindow`, the method that draws it.
+
+It states what it saw and names no cause. Pickle records `Widgets.ButtonText` only, so a control
+drawn some other way does not appear among the controls.
+
+A step of your own can append the same report to its failure message with
+`PickleContext.DescribeLastClick()`, which returns null before any click.
